Adapted files:

  native/aec_ffi.cc
    from packages/cc_natives/native/aec_ffi.cc
    The six-symbol C ABI is preserved symbol-for-symbol; comments are rewritten
    for Audio Kit's near/far terminology.

  lib/src/bindings.dart
    from packages/cc_natives/lib/src/audio/aec/aec_ffi_bindings.dart and
    packages/cc_natives/lib/src/native_library.dart
    The raw symbol surface is unchanged. Library resolution is reworked from an
    application-support data directory to explicit path -> environment variable
    -> conventional locations beside the executable, and the probe failure is a
    structured AecUnavailable carrying the paths tried.

  lib/src/processor.dart
    from packages/cc_natives/lib/src/audio/aec/aec_processor.dart
    Blocks are Int16List rather than Uint8List (Audio Kit converts float32 at
    the block boundary, so no byte order is named); the block-size contract
    throws instead of asserting; AecEngine additionally carries sampleRate and
    blockFrames so a composing filter can reject a mismatched format.

  lib/src/mic_filter.dart
    from lib/features/meetings/data/services/aec_mic_filter.dart
    The four stream-orchestration policies — eager never-paused consumption,
    the reference-availability zero-pad gate, fail-safe passthrough until lock,
    and lock-once-track-forever — are carried over with their constants
    (80 ms target lead, 0.55 lock confidence, 500 ms delay clamp, 500 ms
    calibration interval). Reshaped from a pair of Stream<Uint8List> transforms
    into a single AudioSource that owns both capture sessions, with Audio Kit's
    lifecycle, cancellation, and frame metadata around them. Block accumulation
    and delay estimation are not reimplemented here; they are
    AecBlockAccumulator and AecDelayEstimator in audio_processing.

  tool/build_native.sh
    from scripts/natives/build_aec.sh and scripts/natives/lib/natives_common.sh
    Inlined the three shared helpers it used; installs into a package-local,
    gitignored .native/ directory instead of an application-support root.

Portions of the accompanying test suite are likewise adapted from Control
Center's tests for the same components.

